#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 600.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167931} :activity/id #uuid "92b5fdfc-2225-50d5-b6fe-9d76c920db9c" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048833 :topic/id #uuid "c46bbf50-5eed-5a5c-9851-dfb4b3e5f4ec" :topic/math-academy-id 3196} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167931 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186168039 :tutorial/content "In the earlier topics, we saw that *symmetry* can force many Fourier coefficients to be zero automatically.\nIn particular, if a $2\\pi$-periodic function is *odd*, then its Fourier series has *sine terms only*.\n\nA **Fourier sine series** uses this idea when a function is initially given only on the half-interval, say, $[0,\\pi),$ but we want a full Fourier series on $[-\\pi,\\pi)$ (and then a $2\\pi$-periodic extension to all real $x$).\n\nTo do this, we start with a function $F(x)$ on $[0,\\pi)$ and define its **odd extension** $f(x)$ to $(-\\pi,\\pi)$ by\n![](images/77/776119c1d430a7d50051ae0e00e254f9d22782bc192aa8a0cab9cc227fe460db.svg)\n\nFor example, a function $F(x),$ defined on $x \\in [0,1),$ and its odd extension $f(x)$ to $x \\in (-1,1)$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/2f/2f915ed450be1abf672e3fd86b56c02820514a778a4d4d174409f5bd99da6834.png)\n\nBy construction, $f$ is an *odd* function, meaning $f(-x)=-f(x)$. Because $f$ is odd, its Fourier series on $[-\\pi,\\pi)$ has *sine terms only*:\n\n$$\nf(x)\\sim \\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} b_n\\sin(nx)\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is odd and $\\sin(nx)$ is odd for any $n \\geq 1,$ then $f(x)\\sin(nx)$ must be even.\nSo, the sine coefficients can be computed using the *half-range formula*:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{n} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot 2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo in practice, the workflow is the following:\n\n1\\. Start with $F$ on $[0,\\pi)$ and form the odd extension $f$ on $(-\\pi,\\pi).$\n\n2\\. Compute $b_n$ from the half-range integral on $[0,\\pi).$\n\n3\\. Write the Fourier sine series of $f.$\n\nLet's see some concrete examples." :tutorial/id #uuid "1e10dc0a-145b-598c-837b-7a6a2f858c85" :tutorial/math-academy-id 14652 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "1dcd5d80-021e-5ab2-8637-bf6a5a9faf0e" :step/math-academy-id 595576 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167932}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167932 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166955 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166567 :question/id #uuid "f7af1dba-6300-56ab-93d2-0f3d1b893dad" :question/math-academy-id "e-21809"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5ee3c3f-4289-5e38-a47a-52e5c2ad3817" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049873}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167270} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167271} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315028} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315029} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315030} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315064} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315093} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379568} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379595} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540067}] :knowledge-point/title "Understanding the Odd Extension of a Function"} :step/id #uuid "31f7c3df-5d68-5318-8629-44acb9dd6545" :step/math-academy-id 595577 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167933}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167933 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166956 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166568 :question/id #uuid "1ff70a32-336a-5ff2-bfe8-0df06eec1a7c" :question/math-academy-id "e-21810"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1a85c9c4-8563-55e0-9d4f-7d61d3be6243" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050730} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050929}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167283} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167284} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315033} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315034} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315083} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315087} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379575} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379582} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379589}] :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Sine Coefficients From the Half-Range Formula"} :step/id #uuid "323c5600-b1d6-59c5-b7db-35b5ba7c1c94" :step/math-academy-id 595580}] :activity/title "Fourier Sine Series" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186166991}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046645} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540129} :activity/id #uuid "efb42fa9-f683-5c06-ac0c-717cbb8d0615" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048833 :topic/id #uuid "c46bbf50-5eed-5a5c-9851-dfb4b3e5f4ec" :topic/math-academy-id 3196} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540119 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379595 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "669c79c2-1922-5d4f-8294-a85dd5e7d7f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379597}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379597} :answer-field/id #uuid "62443fee-fe96-5815-bb89-8967be450b9e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379596}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0188791e-a7fa-5d1c-b905-419c47766caf" :question/math-academy-id "q-341203" :question/problem "Let $F(x)={x}^{2}-6x$ for $x\\in [0,12),$ and let $f(x)$ be the **odd** extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in (-12,12).$ What is the value of $f(-4)?$\n\n$f(-4)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [0,12),$ the odd extension of $F$ is the function $f$ such that\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}F(x), & x\\in [0,12), \\\\ -F(-x), & x\\in (-12,0).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, for $x\\in (-12,0),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =-F(-x) \\\\  & =-((-x)^{2}-6(-x)) \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}+6x) \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}-6x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-4) & =-(-4)^{2}-6(-4)=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "0e3afe28-7b8e-5c73-9d90-38ba90dbb6e5" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540166}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540129 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167270 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03bfdb40-b020-5871-af7f-669ab81b634f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-{x}^{2}-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539484} {:answer/id #uuid "0d477725-039a-569b-974c-cc8168427bd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-{x}^{2}+2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539506} {:answer/id #uuid "133cc9fe-58b4-5563-9de2-f20044a1ad82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}^{2}-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539516} {:answer/id #uuid "8d7a4ec2-f370-5681-81e3-c63a1d8a2f8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "|x{|}^{2}+2|x|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539719} {:answer/id #uuid "a721105a-d718-5aac-86a9-455b5f022623" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "|-{x}^{2}+2x|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539760}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186539484} :answer-field/id #uuid "163adf1f-a5ba-53ac-95f1-d113394667f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164819}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "487df78e-b6e4-5124-9586-cb2ed967b312" :question/math-academy-id "q-338784" :question/problem "Let $F(x)={x}^{2}-2x$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi ),$ and let $f(x)$ be the **odd** extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in (-\\pi ,\\pi ).$ What is $f(x)$ for $x\\in (-\\pi ,0)?$" :question/worked-solution "If $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [0,\\pi ),$ the odd extension of $F$ is the function $f$ such that\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}F(x), & x\\in [0,\\pi ), \\\\ -F(-x), & x\\in (-\\pi ,0).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, for $x\\in (-\\pi ,0),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =-F(-x) \\\\  & =-((-x)^{2}-2(-x)) \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}+2x) \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}-2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "39da7f89-1eb5-57a1-96ef-3e5ae3c5298e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540150}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540150 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315033 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2bc2695f-0e15-5691-a028-b150d466dcf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3(-1)^{n}}{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312316} {:answer/id #uuid "725ea555-7d4c-5eaf-95eb-128a98f4ed38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{6(-1)^{n}}{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312872} {:answer/id #uuid "f347fe48-c18b-5b04-9912-af36b33ea06b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{6(1-(-1)^{n})}{\\pi n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313921} {:answer/id #uuid "fa8ec435-d3fb-5f32-883e-f63f94659176" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3(1-(-1)^{n})}{\\pi n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313974}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312872} :answer-field/id #uuid "da0d16eb-266b-580b-b823-2ca3bad44068" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314614} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f25da9e-c33a-5999-a8c4-ac447897722c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312485} {:answer/id #uuid "525fe023-9b2c-5613-ac7a-b31e065a357b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312643} {:answer/id #uuid "b69786fc-4a61-5bdb-88d2-2cf63ec7fbf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313393} {:answer/id #uuid "dfe655ac-4aeb-5468-80b5-b24c11370919" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313735}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312485} :answer-field/id #uuid "ece722c4-3730-5a44-bfa8-824b101a061a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314658}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7f36f74d-9ded-58b3-8942-de350905b5b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-340922" :question/problem "Let $F(x)=-3x$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi ).$ Select the correct missing parts in the Fourier sine series of the **odd** $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of the function $F(x)$ below.\n\n$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-1}}\\cdot {{field-2}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For our Fourier sine series, the coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=-3x$ for $x\\in (0,\\pi ).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=-\\frac{6}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe use the integration by parts: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⇒\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\, & ⇒\\,v=-\\frac{1}{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{n} & =-\\frac{6}{\\pi }(uv\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{\\pi }(-\\frac{1}{n}[x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }+\\frac{1}{n}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{n\\pi }((\\pi \\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-0\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))-\\frac{1}{n}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{n\\pi }(\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-\\frac{1}{n}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))) \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )}{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )=(-1)^{n},$ we have\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=\\frac{6(-1)^{n}}{n}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the Fourier sine series is\n\n$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{6(-1)^{n}}{n}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx).\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "745e2678-3dfd-5d17-a3ad-6185ef0d904f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540119}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540166 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315083 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17d2b4d4-59ed-5f0d-9922-89c02bc8942c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{n\\pi }((-1)^{n}(3\\pi +2)-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312144} {:answer/id #uuid "1c7dfd21-ea92-5be3-8cba-ebde5cac0a85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{n\\pi }((-1)^{n}(3\\pi -2)+2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312186} {:answer/id #uuid "b1ef0a66-4c64-5da9-8e07-1ee81ddb44b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{n\\pi }((-1)^{n}(3\\pi -2)+2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313358} {:answer/id #uuid "e47a9901-72d0-5e49-98e9-0f5ae120d820" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3(1-(-1)^{n})}{\\pi n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313780}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312186} :answer-field/id #uuid "27702b14-e617-57ac-90a9-1bb0c61d35a6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314114} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6441ae36-adf1-5855-b981-8fc098d80d81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312770} {:answer/id #uuid "7389b0c8-c427-5783-917f-54f1d71de35e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312890} {:answer/id #uuid "d3f60e40-1d50-5fed-9993-320e426adf71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313640} {:answer/id #uuid "fe0e894e-bcb8-5db4-8c39-fd7a667523d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314002}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312890} :answer-field/id #uuid "84d7a55f-6b4e-5c7e-90c0-f352d65aa8ea" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314361}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ac9732d3-1086-5e0e-8f66-b1641de82b66" :question/math-academy-id "q-341336" :question/problem "Let $F(x)=-3x+2$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi ).$ Select the correct missing parts in the Fourier sine series of the **odd** $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of the function $F(x)$ below.\n\n$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-1}}\\cdot {{field-2}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For our Fourier sine series, the coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=-3x+2$ for $x\\in (0,\\pi ).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(-3x+2)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe use the integration by parts: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=-3x+2\\, & ⇒\\,{u}^{′}=-3 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\, & ⇒\\,v=-\\frac{1}{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{n} & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }(uv\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }(-\\frac{1}{n}[(-3x+2)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }-\\frac{3}{n}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{n\\pi }(((-3\\pi +2)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))+\\frac{3}{n}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{n\\pi }((-3\\pi +2)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-2+\\frac{3}{n}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{n\\pi }((-3\\pi +2)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )=(-1)^{n},$ we have\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=-\\frac{2}{n\\pi }((-3\\pi +2)(-1)^{n}-2)=\\frac{2}{n\\pi }((-1)^{n}(3\\pi -2)+2).\n$$\n\nFinally, the Fourier sine series is\n\n$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{n\\pi }((-1)^{n}(3\\pi -2)+2)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx).\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "bebe94fc-0239-52b8-b44d-7f460d1d5644" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540171}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540171 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540067 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6bd683e8-a847-5e05-99c1-b681ee2fc285" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539659} {:answer/id #uuid "7027ff52-37a6-5339-8ae8-c81614622435" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "|x{|}^{3}+2|x{|}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539668} {:answer/id #uuid "a982a159-987e-5602-86d9-3a2e2fddf4d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "|-{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539767} {:answer/id #uuid "abed5605-656d-5242-a084-ad7f11b0d696" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539771} {:answer/id #uuid "ef3b5131-7b3a-5bc8-9252-83975f1ec410" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539879}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186539879} :answer-field/id #uuid "149df211-1ed2-522f-a2c8-98bc68e1b2c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539928}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "899a46d0-c395-5e11-8fbc-04b90f756929" :question/math-academy-id "q-341407" :question/problem "Let $F(x)={x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+8$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi ),$ and let $f(x)$ be the **odd** extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in (-\\pi ,\\pi ).$ What is $f(x)$ for $x\\in (-\\pi ,0)?$" :question/worked-solution "If $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [0,\\pi ),$ the odd extension of $F$ is the function $f$ such that\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}F(x), & x\\in [0,\\pi ), \\\\ -F(-x), & x\\in (-\\pi ,0).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, for $x\\in (-\\pi ,0),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =-F(-x) \\\\  & =-((-x)^{3}-2(-x)^{2}+8) \\\\  & =-(-{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+8) \\\\  & ={x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "de01dadb-e088-5a80-88fd-7569dc237f04"}] :activity/title "Fourier Sine Series" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539476}]}
